# LF in the working tree on every OS, whatever `core.autocrlf` says.
#
# ⚠️ Without this a Windows checkout -- including GitHub's `windows-latest` runner, where
# autocrlf is on -- turns every `.sh` into `set -euo pipefail\r`, which bash reads as an
# invalid option, and every generated region `build-index.py --check` compares into a
# permanent diff. The gates would then be red on Windows for a reason that is not in the tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz  binary
